-**Subtopics:**
-*   **Deformable Sampling:** A strategy that employs a learnable offset to adaptively deform sampling positions, forcing density distribution to converge on the target accurate surface [S1]. It is chosen when sample-position confusion ('WHERE to sample?') is the primary issue due to sparse inputs [S1].
-*   **Semi-Supervised NeRF Paradigm:** A paradigm that adopts consistency regularization between unseen rays and perturbed rays generated by pose perturbation to mitigate over-fitting [S1]. It is chosen when prediction confusion ('HOW to predict?') arises from the gap between training and testing viewpoints [S1].
